# Suite tool nav (in-page tabs)

Prefer the refrigeration-style **horizontal tool switcher** on every calculator page inside a suite. Users keep each tool’s form state (separate URLs / pages) but can jump tools without going back to the picker.

## Pattern

1. Partial: `_psychro_tool_nav.html`, `_air_tool_nav.html`, `_hydronics_tool_nav.html`, `_refrig_tool_nav.html`
2. Include at the top of `{% block content %}`:

```jinja
{% with tool='coil' %}
{% include "_psychro_tool_nav.html" %}
{% endwith %}
```

3. CSS class: `.suite-tool-nav` (`.refrig-tool-nav` kept as alias)
4. Each link: long label in `.suite-tool-nav-full`, short in `.suite-tool-nav-short` (mobile swaps via CSS)
5. Coming-soon tools: same strip + `<span class="soon">Soon</span>`
6. Trailing **All** link → suite picker

## Psychro (many tools)

- Use `.suite-tool-nav--psychro.suite-tool-nav--rows` with two `.suite-tool-nav-row` grids (5 + 5).
- Do **not** horizontal-scroll / clip psychro tabs — two fixed rows.
- Keep `.v2-main` wide for the whole psychro suite (`:has(.suite-tool-nav--psychro)`) so switching tools does not change chrome width.

## Mobile (short suites: air / hydronics / refrigeration)

- Do **not** wrap pills into many rows on small screens.
- Horizontal scroll (`overflow-x: auto`, `flex-wrap: nowrap`, touch scrolling).
- Sticky under the fixed V2 topbar (`top: var(--v2-top)`).
- Short labels at `max-width: 720px`.

## Do not

- Replace top-nav suite dropdowns or picker pages — tabs are the *in-suite* switcher only.
- Use a different control style per suite (pills / underline / segmented) — keep one pattern.
- Put suite tabs only on refrigeration; new modules must include the matching partial.
